  "question": {
    "text": "If the solution curve of the differential equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;passes through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> then the abscissa of the point on the curve whose ordinate is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is"
  },
